  "result": "Done! I've implemented payment terms support:\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added TERMS_INVALID \u2014 \"Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\"\n\n**Updated createInvoice:**\n- Now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Validates terms against 'NET14', 'NET30', 'EOM'\n- Calculates due date based on term:\n  - **NET14**: 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - **EOM**: last day of the issue date's month\n- Stores `terms` and `dueDate` on the invoice\n- Uses `addDays()` from dates.js for NET calculations\n\n**Tests:**\n- Added 10 test cases covering:\n  - Default NET30 terms\n  - Explicit NET14 and NET30\n  - EOM calculations (regular months, leap year February, year boundaries)\n  - EOM when issued on last day of month\n  - Invalid terms rejection\n  - Month/year boundary crossing with NET14/NET30\n- All 147 tests pass\n\n**Design:**\n- Due date is calculated and fixed at invoice creation time\n- EOM handles all edge cases including leap years correctly\n- Terms are immutable after invoice is created",
